# UI System Organization Guide

## UI Folder Structure (4 Categories)

### 1. **HealthBar/** - Health and Status UI
**Purpose**: Player health, experience, and status displays
**Files**:
- `LevelUI.cs` - Level display and experience bar
- `ResultPopupController.cs` - Game result popups and notifications

**Guidelines**:
- Handle all health-related UI elements
- Manage experience bar and level progression display
- Control result screens and game over popups
- Update in real-time based on PlayerStats changes

### 2. **SkillUI/** - Skill and Combat UI
**Purpose**: Skill buttons, combat feedback, and ability displays
**Files**:
- `SkillUIController.cs` - Unified skill UI management
- `AttackButtonController.cs` - Attack input handling
- `MagicLaser.cs` - Magic effect visualizations

**Guidelines**:
- Automatically detect character class and show appropriate skills
- Handle skill cooldowns and availability states
- Provide visual feedback for skill activation
- Coordinate with SkillController for skill execution

### 3. **EquipmentUI/** - Inventory and Equipment
**Purpose**: Inventory management, weapon display, and equipment interaction
**Files**:
- `ActiveInventory.cs` - Main inventory system
- `InventorySlot.cs` - Individual inventory slot management
- `WeaponInfo.cs` - Weapon information display
- `MouseFollow.cs` - Item dragging and mouse interaction

**Guidelines**:
- Handle all inventory operations (add, remove, move items)
- Display weapon stats and information
- Manage drag-and-drop functionality
- Integrate with ItemData and weapon systems

### 4. **MenuUI/** - Navigation and Scene Management
**Purpose**: Main menus, scene transitions, and game flow
**Files**:
- `LobbyUIController.cs` - Lobby scene interface
- `LoadingSceneController.cs` - Loading screen management
- `PauseMenuController.cs` - In-game pause functionality

**Guidelines**:
- Control scene transitions (Lobby → Loading → Scene1 → Scene2 → Scene3)
- Handle pause/resume functionality
- Manage main menu navigation
- Provide loading screen feedback

## UI Development Standards

### Component Organization
```csharp
[Header("UI References")]
public Button skillButton;
public Image cooldownOverlay;
public TextMeshProUGUI skillText;

[Header("Settings")]
[Range(0.1f, 5f)]
public float animationDuration = 1f;
```

### Event Handling
```csharp
// Use UnityEvents for Inspector-assignable callbacks
public UnityEvent OnSkillActivated;
public UnityEvent<float> OnHealthChanged;

// Subscribe to events in OnEnable/OnDisable
private void OnEnable()
{
    PlayerStats.OnHealthChanged += UpdateHealthDisplay;
}

private void OnDisable()
{
    PlayerStats.OnHealthChanged -= UpdateHealthDisplay;
}
```

### Animation and Feedback
- Use Unity's Animation system for UI transitions
- Implement smooth transitions between states
- Provide visual feedback for user interactions
- Use consistent animation timing across all UI elements

### Responsive Design
- Support different screen resolutions
- Use Unity's Canvas Scaler for scaling
- Test on various aspect ratios
- Ensure UI elements remain accessible

## Cross-System Integration

### Player System Integration
```csharp
// Connect UI to PlayerStats
public class HealthBarController : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("References")]
    public PlayerStats playerStats;
    public Slider healthSlider;
    public TextMeshProUGUI healthText;
    
    private void Start()
    {
        if (playerStats != null)
        {
            playerStats.OnHealthChanged += UpdateHealthDisplay;
        }
    }
    
    private void UpdateHealthDisplay(float currentHealth, float maxHealth)
    {
        healthSlider.value = currentHealth / maxHealth;
        healthText.text = $"{currentHealth:F0} / {maxHealth:F0}";
    }
}
```

### Weapon System Integration
```csharp
// Connect UI to weapon switching
public class WeaponUIController : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("Weapon Display")]
    public Image weaponIcon;
    public TextMeshProUGUI weaponName;
    
    public void UpdateWeaponDisplay(IWeapon weapon)
    {
        weaponIcon.sprite = weapon.WeaponIcon;
        weaponName.text = weapon.WeaponName;
    }
}
```

### Character Class Integration
```csharp
// Auto-detect character class for skill UI
public class SkillUIController : MonoBehaviour
{
    private void Start()
    {
        DetectCharacterClass();
        SetupSkillUI();
    }
    
    private void DetectCharacterClass()
    {
        if (FindObjectOfType<Warrior>() != null)
        {
            characterClass = CharacterClass.Warrior;
        }
        else if (FindObjectOfType<Assassin>() != null)
        {
            characterClass = CharacterClass.Assassin;
        }
        else if (FindObjectOfType<Wizard>() != null)
        {
            characterClass = CharacterClass.Wizard;
        }
    }
}
```

## Performance Optimization

### UI Performance Guidelines
- Use object pooling for frequently created/destroyed UI elements
- Minimize Layout Group recalculations
- Use Canvas Groups for batch alpha changes
- Separate static and dynamic UI elements into different canvases

### Memory Management
- Unsubscribe from events in OnDestroy
- Use weak references for large UI hierarchies
- Cache UI component references
- Avoid creating UI elements at runtime when possible

## Testing and Quality Assurance

### UI Testing Checklist
- [ ] All UI elements respond to input correctly
- [ ] Transitions are smooth and consistent
- [ ] UI scales properly on different resolutions
- [ ] All text is readable and properly formatted
- [ ] No UI elements overlap or clip
- [ ] Loading screens function properly
- [ ] Menu navigation works as expected

### Character-Specific Testing
- [ ] Warrior skills display correctly
- [ ] Assassin skills display correctly
- [ ] Wizard skills display correctly
- [ ] Weapon switching updates UI properly
- [ ] Health/MP bars update in real-time
- [ ] Inventory operations work smoothly

### Scene Transition Testing
- [ ] Lobby → Loading transition works
- [ ] Loading → Scene1 transition works
- [ ] Scene1 → Scene2 transition works
- [ ] Scene2 → Scene3 transition works
- [ ] Pause menu functions in all scenes
- [ ] Loading screens show proper progress
